# Plan 16 L2 projection rules (issue #1138) — which ES token classes and
# TypeScript-only constructs each source root accepts. The engine
# (rust/src/es_meta.rs) is a generic matcher over this table; nothing here
# is decided in code, so a rule change re-points every renderer at once.
#
# Honest limit, stated where it bites — generic parameter lists (`<T>`)
# cannot be recognized at token-tree fidelity because `a < b > c` is legal
# plain JavaScript, so they carry silently rather than being guessed at.
# An `as` cast signature is excluded for the same reason from the other
# side — `export { x as y }` is plain ES module syntax, so `as` followed
# by an identifier is not TypeScript-only evidence. A fidelity raise or a
# real ./ts corpus owes both recognizers.
#
# Plan 16 L5 declares the root projections here too — one row per directed
# pair of distinct roots, stating the pivot fidelity the projection carries
# and whether it is live or owed by a plan 16 leaf. `rust to meta` is
# `signature` (the self-AST census) and `meta to rust` is `network`, the
# lossless LinkNetwork serialization of plan 16 L7, rendered back with
# `reconstruct_text`. No row marks rust to es live at any fidelity — that
# projection does not exist yet, and a live row saying it would be invented
# coverage; the legs are declared owed by L8 until that leaf delivers them.
language_projection
  description "Token-class and construct projection rules for the plan 16 js ts rust cycle. A token class either carries to a root or is refused there. A ts_construct signature names a leaf and group sequence that cannot be valid plain JavaScript, and refusing it to js is how the ts to js direction stays honest. Generic parameter lists are not recognizable at token fidelity and carry; that gap is deliberate and documented. Root projection rows declare, per directed root pair, the fidelity the pivot carries and the plan 16 leaf that owes any leg not yet live."
  token_class identifier
    carries_to js
    carries_to ts
  token_class numeric
    carries_to js
    carries_to ts
  token_class string
    carries_to js
    carries_to ts
  token_class template_chunk
    carries_to js
    carries_to ts
  token_class regexp
    carries_to js
    carries_to ts
  token_class punctuator
    carries_to js
    carries_to ts
  token_class group
    carries_to js
    carries_to ts
  token_class template
    carries_to js
    carries_to ts
  token_class interpolation
    carries_to js
    carries_to ts
  ts_construct interface_declaration
    signature leaf interface
    signature identifier
    signature group brace
    refuses_to js
  ts_construct enum_declaration
    signature leaf enum
    signature identifier
    signature group brace
    refuses_to js
  ts_construct type_alias
    signature leaf type
    signature identifier
    signature leaf =
    refuses_to js
  ts_construct satisfies_expression
    signature leaf satisfies
    signature identifier
    refuses_to js
  root_projection rust_to_meta
    from rust
    to meta
    fidelity signature
    status live
  root_projection js_to_meta
    from js
    to meta
    fidelity token_tree
    status live
  root_projection ts_to_meta
    from ts
    to meta
    fidelity token_tree
    status live
  root_projection meta_to_js
    from meta
    to js
    fidelity token_tree
    status live
  root_projection meta_to_ts
    from meta
    to ts
    fidelity token_tree
    status live
  root_projection js_to_ts
    from js
    to ts
    fidelity token_tree
    status live
  root_projection ts_to_js
    from ts
    to js
    fidelity token_tree
    status live
  root_projection rust_to_js
    from rust
    to js
    fidelity token_tree
    status live
  root_projection rust_to_ts
    from rust
    to ts
    fidelity token_tree
    status live
  root_projection meta_to_rust
    from meta
    to rust
    fidelity network
    status live
  root_projection js_to_rust
    from js
    to rust
    fidelity token_tree
    status live
  root_projection ts_to_rust
    from ts
    to rust
    fidelity token_tree
    status live
